999
entities.dxf -- HAND-AUTHORED, and it exists because the two fixtures beside it could not
999
see four stages of work. sample.dxf and plate.dxf hold ZERO splines, ZERO bulges and no
999
BLOCKS section at all, so the byte-for-byte digest guard reported "nothing moved" while the
999
renderer's output changed for 29, 26 and 24 real files respectively. Every entity here is a
999
shape one of those stages draws and none of the older fixtures contains.
999
.
999
$INSUNITS 4 is millimetres, so one drawing unit is one millimetre and every number below is
999
the measurement it claims to be. Model space is Y-UP; the payload and the thumbnail both
999
flip it, which is why the job box's height comes out of y = -20..50.
999
.
999
POLYLINE, closed, four vertices -- (0,0) (40,0) (40,20) (0,20). TWO BULGES OF EQUAL SIZE AND
999
OPPOSITE SIGN, which is the whole point of them: b = 1.0 on the bottom edge is a half turn,
999
so that edge is a semicircle of r=20 bulging DOWN to y=-20, and b = -1.0 on the top edge is
999
the same half turn the other way, biting DOWN into the rectangle as far as y=0. Read |b| and
999
the top arc leaves through y=+40 instead -- 20 mm of bbox, in the one direction a
999
sign-blind implementation cannot tell apart. Extent x 0..40, y -20..20.
999
.
999
SPLINE, degree 3, five control points, knots 0,0,0,0,1,2,2,2,2. The interior knot at 1 is
999
what makes this TWO spans rather than one Bezier, so it exercises the span search de Boor
999
needs -- evaluate the second half against the first span and it extrapolates a plausible
999
curve of the wrong shape. Clamped at both ends: the contour starts at (60,0) and ends at
999
(80,0) and peaks at y=15, inside a control polygon spanning x 60..80, y 0..20.
999
.
999
ARC at (120,0), r=10, with start angle == end angle. That is a FULL TURN, not a zero-length
999
arc (Dxf.arc_points says so in as many words), and its start and end points therefore
999
coincide -- which SVG resolves by omitting the segment ENTIRELY. This entity is here so that
999
"a full-circle ARC draws nothing in the thumbnail" (tinkerex#215) has a fixture that fails.
999
.
999
BLOCKS section defining TAB -- a LINE from (0,0) to (10,0) -- and ONE INSERT placing it at
999
(200,50). The offset is non-zero on purpose: at (0,0) a placed block lands exactly where the
999
ghost at its definition coordinates used to draw, so the bug that fix removed would still
999
pass. Drawn once, at (200,50)-(210,50).
999
.
999
JOB BOX: 210 x 70 mm, from x 0..210 and y -20..50. FOUR shapes, in document order:
999
polyline, spline, arc, inserted line -- the block body is not a fifth.
